Subject: [PATCH] fix(models): preserve authored face UV rotations

Read per-face uv_rotation into the shared geometry model and retain it
through cloning, normalization and Java item export. Compose fitted cube
rotations with the authored angle instead of replacing it.

Bedrock added clockwise quarter-turn face UV rotation in geometry format
1.21.0, before the target Bedrock 1.26.51.1/protocol 2193. The 1.26.40
schema retains the four supported angles. This supplies the same parsed
metadata to native actor and skin consumers without changing coordinates.
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/minecraft/creator/reference/content/visualreference/geometry.v1.26.40

Regression controls cover all six faces and all four angles, signed UV
rectangles, absent faces, independent clones, rotation composition,
normalization and Java item export. The original implementation fails
the regression; the complete converter test suite passes after the fix.
